15 0 obj
<< /A 41 0 R /Alt (Graphs showing normalized expression levels of various miRNAs in serum and tissue across different chemotherapy conditions. Panels A and B show data for healthy controls, chemo naive, and treated serum samples, with colors representing each group. Panels C, D, and E detail miRNAs miR-182, miR-130a, and miR-20a, respectively, with expression changes over chemotherapy cycles CT0 to CT3. Panel F shows data for tissue expression in chemonaive and treated patients. Panel G compares expression across paired samples of serum and tissue. Statistically significant differences are indicated with asterisks.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 30 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 42 0 R /Alt (Graph A shows a significant positive correlation between serum and tissue expression of miR-200a \(r = 0.4727, p = 0.0003\). Graph B depicts normalized tissue expression of miR-182, miR-20a, and miR-106a across FIGO stages. Graph C presents serum expression of miR-182, miR-145, miR-200a, and miR-23b based on the presence or absence of metastatic ascites. Graph D shows serum levels of miR-130a and miR-23b, and Graph E displays tissue expression of miR-433 and miR 145, both stratified by metastasis status. Statistically significant differences are marked by asterisks.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 32 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 43 0 R /Alt (Box and violin plots showing normalized expression of selected miRNAs in serum and tissue from ovarian cancer patients. Panels A and B display box plots for miR-182, miR-130a, miR-106a, and miR-23b, comparing Chemotherapy Response Scores \(CRS 1 vs. CRS 2\) using distinct colors and patterns. Panels C and D show violin plots for miR-182, miR-23b, miR-106a, miR-9, and miR 200a, illustrating differences between early and late relapse groups. Panel E includes a correlation table showing associations between CA-125 levels and tissue expression of various miRNAs. Statistically significant differences are indicated with asterisks.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 33 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 44 0 R /Alt (Kaplan-Meier plots depict progression-free survival percentages over 80 months for different conditions. Plot A compares chemo naive versus treated patients. Plot B contrasts FIGO stages I & II with III & IV. Plot C examines low versus high CA-125 levels. Plot D evaluates absent versus present lymph node metastasis. Each graph includes median progression-free survival times and hazard ratios.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 34 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 45 0 R /Alt (Panel A shows combined ROC curves for miR-182, miR-106a, and miR-23b, with corresponding AUC, sensitivity, and specificity values. Panel B displays the combined ROC curve for the same microRNAs with an AUC of 0.743, sensitivity of 0.816, and specificity of 0.605.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 35 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
